Smartmontools SDK — Installation Guide
=======================================

This file describes how to integrate the prebuilt `libsmartmon` library
into your project, and how to build the SDK from source.

For instructions on building the full smartmontools suite (smartctl/smartd),
see the upstream repository: https://github.com/smartmontools/smartmontools


Table of contents:

[1] Using a prebuilt release
[2] Building from source
[3] Cross-compiling
[4] Linking against libsmartmon
[5] Supported platforms


[1] Using a prebuilt release
=============================

Download the archive for your target platform from:
  https://github.com/dianlight/smartmontools-sdk/releases

Each release provides one .tar.gz per target, e.g.:
  libsmartmon-8.0-linux-amd64.tar.gz
  libsmartmon-8.0-darwin-aarch64.tar.gz
  libsmartmon-8.0-windows-amd64.tar.gz

The archive layout is:
  lib/libsmartmon.a
  include/smartmon/

Extract to a prefix of your choice:

  tar -xzf libsmartmon-<version>-<target>.tar.gz -C /usr/local


[2] Building from source
=========================

Requirements:
  - GNU Autoconf >= 2.69
  - GNU Automake >= 1.15
  - GNU Libtool >= 2.4
  - A C++11 compiler (gcc, clang, or MinGW-w64 for Windows cross-builds)
  - Git (for submodule checkout)

Steps:

  git clone --recurse-submodules \
      https://github.com/dianlight/smartmontools-sdk.git
  cd smartmontools-sdk
  ./autogen.sh
  mkdir build && cd build
  ../configure --with-devel=yes
  make -C include
  make -j$(nproc) -C lib libsmartmon.la

Output:
  build/lib/.libs/libsmartmon.a   — static library
  include/smartmon/               — public headers (source tree)

To install to a prefix:
  make -C lib install

To install only the development files (headers + library):
  make -C include install
  make -C lib install-includeHEADERS


[3] Cross-compiling
====================

Use the standard autoconf --host / --build options plus the cross-compiler
CC and CXX variables.

Example — macOS arm64 (using osxcross):
  ../configure --build=$(../config.guess) \
               --host=x86_64-apple-darwin20.4 \
               --with-devel=yes \
               CC=o64-clang CXX=o64-clang++ \
               CFLAGS="-arch arm64" \
               CXXFLAGS="-arch arm64 -stdlib=libc++"

Example — Windows amd64 (MinGW-w64):
  ../configure --build=$(../config.guess) \
               --host=x86_64-w64-mingw32 \
               --with-devel=yes \
               CC=x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc \
               CXX=x86_64-w64-mingw32-g++

Note: When cross-compiling, build only the library target to avoid cross-arch
issues with the examples directory:

  make -j$(nproc) -C lib libsmartmon.la


[4] Linking against libsmartmon
================================

C++ project (Makefile):
  CPPFLAGS += -I/usr/local/include
  LDFLAGS  += -L/usr/local/lib
  LDLIBS   += -lsmartmon -lstdc++

CMake:
  find_library(SMARTMON_LIB smartmon REQUIRED)
  find_path(SMARTMON_INCLUDE smartmon/dev_interface.h REQUIRED)
  target_include_directories(mytarget PRIVATE ${SMARTMON_INCLUDE})
  target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE ${SMARTMON_LIB})

pkg-config (if installed):
  pkg-config --cflags --libs smartmon

Key public headers under include/smartmon/:
  dev_interface.h    — device abstraction (open, identify, passthrough)
  atacmds.h          — ATA/SATA commands
  nvmecmds.h         — NVMe commands
  json.h             — JSON output builder
  utility.h          — logging and string helpers
  smartmon_defs.h    — common macros and type definitions


[5] Supported platforms
========================

  OS          Architecture   Toolchain
  --------    -------------- -------------------------------------------
  Linux       amd64          gcc/g++
  Linux       aarch64        aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc/g++ (cross)
  macOS       amd64          osxcross o64-clang (cross, -arch x86_64)
  macOS       aarch64        osxcross o64-clang (cross, -arch arm64)
  Windows     amd64          x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc/g++ (cross)

Additional information:
  https://github.com/dianlight/smartmontools-sdk
